cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tactix, please cite it as below."
title: "Tactix: a SAT solver with a programmable strategy interface"
abstract: >-
  Tactix is a proof-producing CDCL SAT solver whose solving strategy is
  programmable through a C interface. Every solver step and inprocessing
  technique is a proof rule that a strategy can select and configure; every
  UNSAT answer comes with a machine-checkable proof. The repository is also
  the artifact of the paper "Tactix: Towards a Programmable Strategy
  Interface for Flexible SAT-Solving".
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ai-ar-research/Tactix"
keywords:
  - SAT solving
  - CDCL
  - proof checking
  - programmable strategy
